context
    # <TICKET-ID>

    Branch name:
    `<branch-name>`

    Implementation Summary:

    - Fix / implementation: <short paragraph: what now happens when the user acts, a brief example when useful, then how the app makes it happen; simple sentences in event order>
    - Root cause: <short paragraph: what the app did before, the missing or incorrect action, and the problem the user saw; simple sentences in event order, or None>

    Code Layer Impact:

    - Impacted services: <repository names without owner/organization prefixes, or None>
    - Core modules/sections: <affected modules or sections>

    UI Impact:

    - New/updated components, layouts, or pages: <affected UI or None>

    DB Impact:

    - New/updated tables: <affected tables or None>
    - Indexing added/updated: <affected indexes or None>

    Infra Impact:

    - Env changes: <environment changes or None>
    - Cloudflare/S3/Redis or other infra changes: <infrastructure changes or None>
as @summary_template

use ../knowledge/summary-knowledge.flow
use ../knowledge/common-knowledge.flow
use ../knowledge/draft-knowledge.flow

do Resolve the explicit project or current checkout and active ticket from
    @request or conversation. Reject supplied-ID mismatches. Return an object
    with project, ticket_id (null if unknown), and ticket (complete matching
    cached Jira object or null). as @task_context

if @task_context.ticket_id == null
    ask "Which Jira ticket should this work use?" as @ticket_input
    do Validate @ticket_input against the active task and return @task_context
        updated with that one Jira ID. as @task_context

set project = @task_context.project
set ticket_id = @task_context.ticket_id
set ticket = @task_context.ticket

do Retain the verified project, ticket ID, and any complete cached ticket as
    this conversation's active task without remote calls or task files.

do Resolve and read the technical-summary.md draft for @project and @ticket_id under
    @draft_rules. Allow a new draft only when none is known.
    Return an object with path and text (both null for a new draft). as @draft_state

set draft_path = @draft_state.path
set saved_draft = @draft_state.text

if @ticket == null
    use ../knowledge/tool-knowledge.flow
    do Resolve private absolute acli using @tool_guidance. Return its path. as @acli
    run @acli jira workitem view @ticket_id --fields "key,issuetype,summary,status,assignee,description,attachment" --json as @ticket_result
    do Parse @ticket_result.stdout as JSON, verify its key equals @ticket_id and
        requested details are complete, and retain the full ticket and project.
        Return the complete object. as @ticket

do Inspect branch and HEAD in @project before reusing earlier code evidence. Resolve the
    requested implementation scope. Return an object with scope and
    scope_is_clear. Wording edits need no code investigation. as @scope_state

if @scope_state.scope_is_clear == false
    ask "Which changes or commit range should this technical summary cover?" as @summary_scope

    do Resolve @summary_scope into a valid implementation scope. Return an
        object with scope and scope_is_clear. as @scope_state

    if @scope_state.scope_is_clear == false
        return "Technical-summary generation stopped because the scope is unclear."

do Review relevant local changes or the explicitly identified commit range in
    @scope_state.scope. Follow exact imports or symbols only for material gaps.
    Do not choose a PR target, fetch, require a clean tree, create commits, or
    run tests solely to write prose. Distinguish observed checks from proposed
    verification. Return the evidence and material uncertainty. as @evidence

do Prepare the summary from @summary_template using @ticket, @saved_draft,
    @evidence, @writing_guidance, and @summary_rules. A new draft has a # TICKET-ID
    heading and the summary body, without PR title or Description headings.
    Preserve an existing draft's layout, accurate notes, and unrequested content.
    Return an object with draft and unrelated_gaps. as @summary_draft

do Verify the requested content in @summary_draft.draft is supported, complete,
    and placeholder-free while preserving accurate developer judgments.

do Save @summary_draft.draft to the technical-summary draft under @draft_rules,
    using @draft_path when present and @saved_draft as the concurrent-edit
    baseline. Verify the active project and ticket still match @project and
    @ticket_id. For a new file allocate only its unique external temporary
    directory. Verify the saved content once and return the absolute path. as @draft_path

print Report @draft_path, @evidence, and @summary_draft.unrelated_gaps briefly.
